<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Empire of China (1915-1916)</h1><p class="st-meta">1915 CE – 1916 CE · capital Beijing</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Yuan Shikai's attempt to make himself emperor of China, which lasted only 83 days and plunged the country into the warlord era.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-shikai">Yuan Shikai</a>, president of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-china">Republic of China</a>, had dissolved parliament and concentrated power. Encouraged by supporters who argued that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> needed a monarchy, and after staged petitions from provincial assemblies, he accepted the throne in December 1915 and adopted the reign title Hongxian from 1 January 1916.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The monarchy changed little in practice, as government continued through the existing ministries of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/beiyang-government">Beiyang government</a>. It was deeply unpopular: Yuan's acceptance of most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan's</a> Twenty-One Demands in 1915 had already damaged him, and Japan and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> disapproved of the restoration.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In December 1915 Cai E and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/later-tang">Tang</a> Jiyao rose in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yunnan">Yunnan</a> in the National Protection War, and other southern provinces declared independence. Losing the support of his own generals, Yuan abandoned the monarchy on 22 March 1916 and died in June, leaving the warlords to divide <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/empire-of-china-1915-1916.jpg" alt="Empire of China (1915-1916)" width="320" height="226"><figcaption>Image: SY · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:China_Dynasties.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1915 CE – 1916 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Beijing</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Yuan Shikai</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Chinese folk religion, Confucianism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Mandarin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/china">China</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hongxian Empire, Empire of China (Yuan Shikai)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1916&amp;focus=empire-of-china-1915-1916" aria-label="Empire of China (1915-1916) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7388 747 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Empire of China (1915-1916) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7708 1003L7868 1006"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7868 1006h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7708 1003h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7708 1003h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1916&amp;focus=empire-of-china-1915-1916">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
